From eb1135f7849e5cfd057b27edd96159692f376bea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 7 Apr 2026 22:40:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HighPriorityMisc: disable ColorFade to avoid system_server
 boot hang

on certain MTK vendor HWC blobs (confirmed on MT6789 in the
Blackview Shark 8) the screen-on color fade animation hangs the
calling thread indefinitely inside BLASTBufferQueue.nativeCreate()
called from ColorFade.prepare(). after 60 seconds the watchdog
kills system_server with the stack trace pointing at
DisplayPowerController.animateScreenStateChange ->
prepareColorFade -> ColorFade.createSurfaceControl ->
BLASTBufferQueue.nativeCreate. system_server respawns, hits the
exact same hang on the same code path, gets killed again, and
the device is left in a crash-respawn loop. user 0 never reaches
RUNNING_UNLOCKED, ACTION_BOOT_COMPLETED never broadcasts, every
window stays hidden, every task stays sleeping, and the screen
appears to be black even though the panel hardware is fully
initialised. visually identical to a backlight failure but the
actual cause is the framework never finishing boot.

set config_displayColorFadeDisabled=true in HighPriorityMisc so
DisplayPowerController constructs with mColorFadeEnabled=false
and the prepareColorFade path is skipped entirely. the hang goes
away, system_server completes boot, the framework reaches
mBootCompleted=true, all the downstream lifecycle events fire,
and the screen actually shows the launcher. the only user-visible
difference is that the brief fade-in/fade-out animation when the
screen turns on or off is replaced by an instant transition,
which is a fair trade for actually being able to use the device.
---
 HighPriorityMisc/res/values/config.xml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/HighPriorityMisc/res/values/config.xml b/HighPriorityMisc/res/values/config.xml
index 7988c1f..9941c06 100644
--- a/HighPriorityMisc/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/HighPriorityMisc/res/values/config.xml
@@ -5,4 +5,11 @@
     <!-- Flag indicating whether platform level volume adjustments are enabled for remote sessions
          on grouped devices. -->
     <bool name="config_volumeAdjustmentForRemoteGroupSessions">true</bool>
+    <!-- disable ColorFade screen-on/off animation. on certain MTK and other vendor
+         HWC blobs the BLAST buffer queue creation inside ColorFade.prepare() hangs
+         indefinitely, watchdog kills system_server, and the device gets stuck in
+         a crash-respawn loop with mBootCompleted=false and mAwake=false. without
+         this override the screen never appears to turn on. cosmetic fade animation
+         loss is a fair trade for actually completing boot. -->
+    <bool name="config_displayColorFadeDisabled">true</bool>
 </resources>
-- 
2.53.0

